+# Legacy Radio 1.4 bridge tests
+
+Build `m86-radio14-test` with the m86 userdebug product. The executable is installed
+under `data/nativetest64/m86-radio14-test`, not included in vendor.img.
+
+The fixture compiles the real RIL request bookkeeping and HAL bridge together,
+uses generated 1.4 response/indication stubs and a fake vendor onRequest callback,
+and never connects to a real modem or registers a binder service. This avoids
+interposing two copies of libril's global objects in the same executable.
+
+The 109 assertions cover static dual-slot card mapping, invalid application counts,
+network-mode bitmap conversion, identical serials on different slots completed out
+of order, request-specific callbacks versus inherited callbacks, legacy data-call
+arguments and roaming protocol selection, rejection of IWLAN handover, IP-list
+conversion, unavailable signal measurements, zero-length responses, and old-client
+callback fallback. The additional m86 cases verify the measured 60-byte SITRIL
+layout, poisoned unused words, LTE/TD-SCDMA offsets, solicited and unsolicited
+1.4 dispatch, malformed lengths, other RIL versions and input-buffer preservation. `radio14_mocks.h` was generated from the platform's 1.4 HIDL
+headers; unused callbacks simply return Void.
+
+A passing fixture establishes conversion/dispatch behavior, not modem operation,
+SIM detection, network attachment, calls, emergency calls or IMS interoperability.
